CORE
noorder.c
--nondet-volatile-write-model A:observe_A --nondet-volatile-write-model B:observe_B --mmio-weak --mmio-early-ack
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
A observed before B: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
Without a barrier the writes to A and B may be observed in either order, so the
device can observe B before A and the ordering assertion fails. Compare
test.desc, where a DMB restores the ordering.
